# Run with: time kanso play map_put_then_read_resorts.kso
#      and: time kanso play map_put_then_read_resorts.kso --interp
#
# Should: run in time linear (or n log n) in the number of operations on
# every engine; each step is one put and one read on a map of at most
# 20,000 int keys.
# Does: the interpreter finishes in 0.06 s; `kanso play` natively takes
# 7.7 s (2.3 s user), and the gap grows with the square of the map. callgrind on the
# port's Myers diff (delta/myers.kso, which alternates `put v k x` with
# `v[k + 1]` reads) puts 80% of all instructions in k_map_sort_build,
# k_msort_cmp and k_key_cmp: a read after a put re-sorts the whole map.
# On a 3,000-line file with 60 changed lines `ugit diff` takes 3.3 s as a
# dev binary, 4.0 s as a release binary, and 0.4 s on the interpreter.
fn walk m i n acc
  return acc if n < i
  grown = put m i (i * 2)
  walk grown (i + 1) n (acc + grown[i - 1 + 1])

print "{walk {} 1 20000 0}"
